{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c81bffe4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "we will begin by importing the modules that we would require in order to create a matrix though there a multitude of ways on how to go about doing do without having to import a seperate library but for this, we will be using numpy specifically."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 397,
   "id": "743c0dca",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import random"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9d43dff8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "initially we will be selecting the value for our modular operator which could be selected randomly but it will heavily influence the output that we will end up getting."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 398,
   "id": "3759d562",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "q = 13"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "80fea41e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Okay next lets create our public key matrix and to not complicate it too much, we will be creating a very simple matrix."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 399,
   "id": "99b8f3d7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# we will call the public key matrix sk and our integer matrix as A\n",
    "A = np.random.randint(0, q, size=(3, 3))\n",
    "sk = np.random.randint(-1, 2, size=(3, 1))  # values in {-1, 0, 1}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f56c6993",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "let us now introduce some error though one should keep in mind to use very small numbers as errors as to not introduce too much noise for the output"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 400,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# we will be using the variable e as the error matrix\n",
    "e = np.random.randint(-1, 2, size=(3, 1))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "64ab05c4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now that we have all the matrices that we require, we will be implementing the formula: b = <A, sk> , i.e, just describes multiplication of two matrices or rather their dot products"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 401,
   "id": "480954be",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# we will be using b as the output variable\n",
    "b = np.matmul(A,sk)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5141e938",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "lets finally introduce some error into the equation and also make use of the modulo opertor that we defined at the beginning of our code"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 402,
   "id": "fc8dad9f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "The output is: \n",
      " [[10]\n",
      " [ 0]\n",
      " [ 2]]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "b = np.add(b,e)\n",
    "b = b%q\n",
    "print(\"The output is: \\n\", b)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2a28914c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "let us now perform decryption; b - A·s mod q"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 403,
   "id": "391cf83e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "d = (b-(np.matmul(A,sk)))%q\n",
    "print(d)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 404,
   "id": "3f8a2d26",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "0\n",
      "0\n",
      "0\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "bit_select = []\n",
    "for i in d:\n",
    "    if(i>q/2):\n",
    "        print(1)\n",
    "        bit_select.append(1)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print(0)\n",
    "        bit_select.append(0)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3439e5fd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "now let us add a decryption scheme"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c8c8317d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Message bit sent: 0\n",
      "Recovered bit: 0\n",
      "Correct: True\n",
      "message: 0\n",
      "e used: 0\n",
      "d_single: 0\n",
      "recovered: 0\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "bit = random.choice(bit_select)\n",
    "a_row = A[0]  # single row\n",
    "b_single = (np.dot(a_row, sk.flatten()) + e[0,0] + bit*(q//2)) % q\n",
    "d_single = (b_single - np.dot(a_row, sk.flatten())) % q\n",
    "if q/4 < d_single < 3*q/4:\n",
    "    recovered_bit = 1\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    recovered_bit = 0\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fef50583",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(f\"Message bit sent: {bit}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Recovered bit: {recovered_bit}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Correct: {bit == recovered_bit}\")\n",
    "print(f\"message: {bit}\")\n",
    "print(f\"e used: {e[0,0]}\")\n",
    "print(f\"d_single: {d_single}\")\n",
    "print(f\"recovered: {recovered_bit}\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
